{"conjecture": "Populations of executables evolved against adversarial property-based oracles will reliably converge to specifications-satisfying code if and only if the oracle suite is itself co-evolved to maximize mutation-kill coverage of the current population — fixed oracle suites inevitably permit semantic drift into passing-but-wrong solutions. The co-evolutionary pressure must be asymmetric: oracles are selected for detecting divergences between high-fitness individuals, while executables are selected for passing the oracle suite with minimal computational cost. Under this dynamic, the population's consensus behavior becomes an executable specification that holds its commitments more faithfully than any hand-written oracle, because the oracle itself is continuously sharpened against the very failures it fails to catch."}
